{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "type": "bugfix",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The manifest explicitly included only Hadamard data, while the JIT loader needs native source files beneath the installed exllamav3 package.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_24bc0b33faf34b3e906f5d8966c8bccc", "call_167ba4e9c236419a8e67ecbfbc4e6055"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "Explicitly including the extension tree addresses the source-availability requirement of deferred compilation without requiring installation-time precompilation.",
      "basis": "inference",
      "evidence": ["call_24bc0b33faf34b3e906f5d8966c8bccc", "call_d53216550bb3407b9763631130a9286b", "call_167ba4e9c236419a8e67ecbfbc4e6055"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "The change adds recursive inclusion of the entire extension directory, preserves Hadamard-data inclusion, and leaves compiler configuration and runtime loading unchanged.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_24bc0b33faf34b3e906f5d8966c8bccc"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [],
  "limitations": [
    "No distribution build, installation, or JIT compilation was executed; actual archive and wheel contents remain unverified.",
    "A scalar computation would not validate this packaging change; its meaningful check requires building and inspecting installation artifacts."
  ],
  "links": ["543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff"],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "packaging",
      "title": "Ship native sources for deferred compilation",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "MANIFEST.in adds `recursive-include exllamav3/exllamav3_ext *`. Unlike a compilation-unit-only filter, this requests the whole nested extension tree, allowing supporting files as well as native compilation units to accompany the package.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_24bc0b33faf34b3e906f5d8966c8bccc"]
        },
        {
          "text": "setup.py enables include_package_data and disables precompilation whenever EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE is present, regardless of its value. With precompilation enabled and Torch available, it instead supplies CUDAExtension and BuildExtension to setuptools.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_d53216550bb3407b9763631130a9286b"]
        },
        {
          "text": "At runtime, ext.py first imports exllamav3_ext. On ModuleNotFoundError it walks the extension directory relative to its own installed file, collects .c, .cpp and .cu files, and passes them to torch.utils.cpp_extension.load together with that directory as an include path. The manifest addition supports this existing fallback rather than changing how compilation is selected.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_167ba4e9c236419a8e67ecbfbc4e6055", "call_24bc0b33faf34b3e906f5d8966c8bccc"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The earlier installation entry documents both precompiled and EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE installation paths and notes the original manifest's Hadamard-data inclusion.",
          "basis": "ancestor",
          "evidence": ["call_13d8559dc82247818dca80f94a892630"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Explicitly includes the native extension tree in the package manifest to support the existing JIT-compilation fallback."
}
